# Supervised Learning

##  Introduction

Supervised Learning is a type of Machine Learning in which a model is trained using labelled data. It learns the relationship between input features and their corresponding outputs to make predictions on new, unseen data.

In this section, I explore different Supervised Learning algorithms, understand their working principles, implement them using Python, and apply them to practical datasets.

##  Learning Objectives

- Understand the fundamentals of Supervised Learning.
- Explore Regression and Classification techniques.
- Understand the mathematical concepts behind each algorithm.
- Build models using Scikit-learn.
- Evaluate model performance using appropriate metrics.
- Apply algorithms to practical Machine Learning projects.

##  Categories of Supervised Learning

### 1. Regression

Regression algorithms are used to predict continuous numerical values.

Algorithms to be explored:

- [x] Linear Regression
- [ ] Multiple Linear Regression
- [ ] Polynomial Regression
- [ ] Ridge Regression
- [ ] Lasso Regression
- [ ] Elastic Net Regression
